<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15039" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ebŏra</span></b> , ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A castle in Spain</i>, perh. the present <i>Ixar</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 1, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				16, 4, 2</span></i>: ex conjec. Turneb. (Bait.
			Baream).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A municipium in Lusitania</i>, also called Libertas
			Julia, now <i>Ebora</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 1,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 22, 35, §
		117</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
